From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] virt: allow a small high PCIe window, right above RAM

On Apple M1 and M2, HVF gives a VM a 36-bit IPA space (64 GiB). The virt
machine puts its high IO regions at 256 GiB or more, so on these Macs the
high PCIe window never fits and QEMU drops it without a word. Every BAR
then shares the 751 MiB window below 1 GiB, where Venus's host memory BAR
(1 GiB and more, aligned to its size) does not fit: the firmware maps no
PCI device at all.

highmem-mmio-size now takes any power of two from 1 GiB. A size below the
default 512 GiB also puts the high IO regions right above RAM instead of
at 256 GiB. With 16 GiB and a 4 GiB VM the window is 16-32 GiB, inside
36 bits. The default layout is unchanged.

--- a/hw/arm/virt.c
+++ b/hw/arm/virt.c
@@ -2574,7 +2574,12 @@
         error_report("maxmem/slots too huge");
         exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
     }
-    if (base < vms->memmap[VIRT_MEM].base + LEGACY_RAMLIMIT_BYTES) {
+    /*
+     * OmacVM: a high PCIe window smaller than the default goes right above
+     * RAM, so it fits a 36-bit IPA space (Apple M1/M2 under HVF: 64 GiB).
+     */
+    if (base < vms->memmap[VIRT_MEM].base + LEGACY_RAMLIMIT_BYTES &&
+        extended_memmap[VIRT_HIGH_PCIE_MMIO].size >= DEFAULT_HIGH_PCIE_MMIO_SIZE) {
         base = vms->memmap[VIRT_MEM].base + LEGACY_RAMLIMIT_BYTES;
     }
 
@@ -3391,11 +3396,9 @@
         return;
     }
 
-    if (size < DEFAULT_HIGH_PCIE_MMIO_SIZE) {
-        char *sz = size_to_str(DEFAULT_HIGH_PCIE_MMIO_SIZE);
-        error_setg(errp, "highmem-mmio-size cannot be set to a lower value "
-                         "than the default (%s)", sz);
-        g_free(sz);
+    /* OmacVM: down to 1 GiB; below 512 GiB it sits right above RAM. */
+    if (size < GiB) {
+        error_setg(errp, "highmem-mmio-size cannot be smaller than 1 GiB");
         return;
     }
 
@@ -4267,7 +4270,9 @@
                                    NULL, NULL);
     object_class_property_set_description(oc, "highmem-mmio-size",
                                           "Set the high memory region size "
-                                          "for PCI MMIO");
+                                          "for PCI MMIO (at least 1 GiB; "
+                                          "below 512 GiB it sits right "
+                                          "above RAM)");
 
     object_class_property_add(oc, "virtio-mmio-transports", "uint8",
                                    virt_get_virtio_transports,
